artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider the Weihrauch lattice, whose elements are equivalence classes of (multi-valued) partial functions f:⊆X⇉Y between represented spaces under Weihrauch reducibility ≤_W (where f ≤_W g iff there exist computable functionals H,K such that whenever G realizes g, the map p ↦ H(p, G(K(p))) realizes f). On this structure one considers the following operations:

- the binary supremum ⊔ and infimum ⊓ with respect to ≤_W;
- the parallel product × (taking (f, g) to f × g acting componentwise);
- the finite-parallelization ∗ (with f^∗ = ⊔_{n∈ℕ} f^{(n)});
- the compositional product ⋆ (with f ⋆ g being the maximum, under ≤_W, of all composites f' ∘ g' with f' ≤_W f, g' ≤_W g);
- the diamond operator ⋄ (the iteration / total-Kleene-star operation);
- the implication → defined via f → g = max_{≤_W} { h : g ≤_W f ⋆ h };
- the constant 1 (the identity on a one-point space);
- the operator b (the "first-order part" / boundedness operator, assigning to each problem f its largest first-order Weihrauch degree below f).

It is known that ⊔ and ⊓ are definable from ≤_W; that ∗ is definable from 1, ≤_W and ×; that ⋄ is definable from 1, ≤_W and ⋆; and that → is definable from ⋆ and ≤_W.

Question: Is the operator b definable from the remaining structure (i.e., from ≤_W together with the operations 1, ×, ⋆, ⋄, →, ⊔, ⊓)?

